{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2576 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "bfb0c1a8cc7b24a8cff4ac510dc988a823b8ca95d8256e87ccfb211dc71da8ac" :edb/db-before-t 2575 :edb/db-after-t 2576 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535888 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:00:11.254Z" 13194139535888 true] [17592186096529 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372693 13194139535888 true] [17592186281875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372692 13194139535888 true] [17592186372692 1034 "7" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535888 true] [17592186372692 1111 #uuid "510f8494-5958-5cca-83ba-93db0b677a6b" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372694 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1089 "q-80139" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1100 "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1113 #uuid "44a821f8-71fd-5b81-8104-bbf058394911" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372693 1145 "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =1+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =4 \\\\ R & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372695 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372696 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372697 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372698 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372699 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1041 "selection" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372696 13194139535888 true] [17592186372694 1110 #uuid "28d0c73e-8e7a-52a7-afbf-abd2325b9421" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372695 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535888 true] [17592186372695 1111 #uuid "6533a720-07a1-5e1f-96f6-d5f1c1463a30" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372696 1034 "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535888 true] [17592186372696 1111 #uuid "a89c0c94-80d1-5507-bdb8-8f743f468818" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372697 1034 "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})" 13194139535888 true] [17592186372697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194